# Secrets
.env

# Photos — copied from Drive at import time. Photographs of the garments stay
# out; generated renders go in, because they are the pictures every screen and
# every design session actually draws.
#
#   photos/Retail/  the 500px retail render thumbnails, ~20 KB each, 4.5 MB all up
#   photos/items/   renders Max uploads for a single garment, 700px each. The
#                   answer to the 61 garments that have none and draw as a
#                   colour swatch on four screens.
#   photos/fits/    the fit renders at full size, 158 MB, plus their thumbs.
#                   Full size and not thumbs alone: the fit modal serves
#                   hero_image_path, so a clone with only thumbs shows a broken
#                   image the moment anyone opens a fit.
#
# Out: photos/originals/ (2.4 GB of photographs) and photos/thumbs/ (their
# thumbnails) — real pictures of Max's clothes, and nothing needs them in git.
photos/*
!photos/Retail/
!photos/fits/
!photos/items/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# Editors
.idea/
.vscode/

# OS
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store

# Generated export — regenerate with scripts/export_wardrobe.py
export/

# Patch artefacts — the pre-patch original is in git history
*.bak
*.new

# Unzipped drops — the files that matter are copied into data/ and docs/
.incoming/

# Import run logs — the run says what it did on screen; the file is scratch
*.log
